{{ template "agent-instructions.md" (dict "self" "claude" "root" .) }}
- Sandbox/permission questions (why a path/command/domain is blocked, how to allow
  it): read `~/.claude/docs/sandbox.md` before spawning a lookup agent.
- Model/tier & subscription-limit questions (pins, subagent tiers, the cross-model
  bridge on pi): read `~/.claude/docs/harness.md` before spawning a lookup agent.
- As the driver, when a body of work is ready to hand back and it touches a
  high-stakes surface (auth or security boundaries, data loss or migration,
  concurrency, an external contract) or spans roughly five or more files, run
  the `cross-model-review` skill once per body of work — unprompted, alongside
  the fresh-eyes subagent pass, never instead of it. The cross-model reviewer
  proposes; you stay the implementer: substantiate each finding independently,
  fix only what survives, and say which you dropped and why.{{/* cross_model_review: yield tracks risk and breadth, not change count; a reviewer that rewrites the program degrades stronger work and a false finding can anchor the implementer, so findings stay hypotheses; the trigger sits in the always-loaded line because the skill body loads only after the model decides to fire (audit log 2026-09-23) */}}
- As the driver, before committing to an architecture or approach decision that
  is expensive to reverse, or when a bug resists a second diagnosis, get a
  decorrelated read via `cross-model-advice` — unprompted, and before presenting a
  plan for approval, not after.{{/* cross_model_advice: reversal cost is highest before implementation, and a cross-model reviewer cannot discard working code when none exists yet */}}
- As the driver, give each Workflow `agent()` its roster `agentType` (no model
  or effort), a narrow file-bounded scope and distilled inputs; size the fan-out
  to the ask; a repeat review starts from the last findings, covering only changes.{{/* workflow_burn: workflow agents were 67% of a measured week's Claude usage (2026-09-26); cost is agent count x lifetime x read volume, 92% cache, which effort barely moves; agentType inherits the roster's tier and effort */}}
